# D20 — the Q5 board-value port: DCT-include-precedence + the decoded divergent pins
# Spec: .specs/bob-m4-board-port.md §3.2 (D20). Task: .specs/forge-m4-task.md.
#
# THE MECHANISM FIRST (§3.2 "the single most important implementation fact"): DrvGen
# regenerates the DCT headers from q5/dct/dct/codegen.dws into the O dir at EVERY
# build (archprepare -> tools/dct/DrvGen; scripts/drvgen/drvgen.mk via
# arch/arm/Makefile:298) and the O-dir copy is the ONLY /inc dir on the compile
# path -- verified live: build-beta-touch-lcm's .pmic_drv.o.cmd / .sd.o.cmd /
# .accdet.o.cmd / .hal_kpd.o.cmd all resolve cust_eint.h etc. from
# -I<objtree>/arch/arm/mach-mt6582/q5/dct/dct/inc. Editing the source-tree
# headers alone would be a silent no-op. D20 therefore adds
#     -I$(MTK_PROJECT_PATH_ROOT)/dct/dct/inc   BEFORE   -I$(DRVGEN_OUT)/inc
# to drivers/misc/mediatek/Makefile.custom (consumed by both the mediatek driver
# tree and arch/arm/mach-mt6582, whose Makefile includes Makefile.custom), and
# maintains the Q5-pinned values IN THE SOURCE HEADERS. DrvGen still runs
# (unused for the three overridden headers); every other header keeps resolving
# from DrvGen and stays bit-identical to today. build/62 asserts the pinned
# values AND proves the precedence took effect on the compiled outputs.
#
# VALUE SOURCES: every constant was re-decoded this session from the pinned
# Lithium kernel blob (kernel.img 5217dd41..., decomp d284ba16..., base
# 0xc0008000; symbols lithium.elf/lithium.syms) -- forge-m4-report §2 carries the
# full VA trail. Nothing copied blindly; several spec-row values were corrected
# by the re-decode (documented below and in the report).
#
# PORTED (priority order per §3.2):
#  1. MSDC1 card-detect: CUST_EINT_MSDC1_INS_NUM 8->3, _DEBOUNCE_CN 1->0
#     (cust_eint.h). Blob: mt_eint_mask(3) @c04f0258, set_hw_debounce(3,0)
#     @c04f02d8, mt_eint_registration(3, LOW(8)|HIGH(4) by sd_cd_polarity,
#     msdc1_eint_handler @0xc04f0344, auto-unmask=1) @c04f02fc; pad triple on
#     GPIO3|0x80000000 mode0/dir0/out0 @c04f0268-84. The fork's msdc1_hw IS the
#     SD+CD-PIN variant (no CONFIG_MTK_WCN_CMB_SDIO_SLOT in q5_defconfig ->
#     board.c #else branch: flags CD_PIN_EN|REMOVABLE, host_function MSDC_SD,
#     cd_level MSDC_CD_LOW) so the fork registers CD channel 8 TODAY -- watching
#     GPIO8, the Q5's SPEAKER pad (false card events). Trigger LOW(8)=/HIGH(4)-
#     by-polarity arms match the fork's msdc1_eint_handler logic byte-for-byte
#     (sd.c set_polarity LOW/HIGH pairs) — only the channel + debounce port.
#     NEW GPIO_MSDC1_EINT_PIN = GPIO3 (GPIO3|0x80000000) + the vendor's
#     mode0/dir-in/out-low triple ported into msdc_enable_cd_irq's enable arm
#     (sd.c) gated on the same CD-wired condition the vendor uses, so the
#     registered channel actually watches the card line like the vendor build.
#  2. ACCDET: CUST_EINT_ACCDET_NUM 0->4 (cust_eint.h),
#     GPIO_ACCDET_EINT_PIN GPIO0->GPIO4 (cust_gpio_usage.h). Blob: probe setup
#     @c04a355c-78 = mode0/dir-in/pull-disable on 0x80000004 -- identical calls
#     to the fork's accdet.c:487-489; mt_eint_set_hw_debounce(4,256) @c04a357c
#     (= CUST_EINT_ACCDET_DEBOUNCE_CN 256, unchanged); registration(4,
#     TRIGGER_LOW(8)=CUST_EINT_ACCDET_TYPE, accdet_eint_func, auto=0)
#     @c04a358c. NOTE (re-decode correction to the spec row): the blob's
#     accdet_eint_func ALSO toggles GPIO7 (0x80000007) for the auxadc/headset
#     switch — the fork's accdet.c compiles NO such consumer (GPIO_FSA8049_PIN
#     undefined; init hook #ifdef'd out; the fork's eint-func has the
#     polarity/debounce re-arm but not the GPIO toggle). GPIO7 is NOT ported
#     (would compile in a one-shot init toggle without the runtime toggle pair
#     -- a half-feature); flagged in forge-m4-report §4 for Bob's D-id if the
#     on-device audio-jack behavior ever needs it.
#  3. OTG: NO PORT — a106 GPIO_OTG_IDDIG_EINT_PIN GPIO17 == blob (mt_usb_otg_init
#     @c0545b34-68: mode0/dir-in/pull-up on GPIO17|0x80000011, eint_set_sens(17,1)
#     + debounce(17,64) + registration(17, LOW, ..., 0) — all chip/USB-subsystem
#     values, not board pins). GPIO_OTG_DRVVBUS_PIN: the blob's VBUS path has NO
#     GPIO at all -- mt_usb_set_vbus @c0544524 selects charger-IC OTG boost
#     (bct24157_set_otg_en/cf40 or fan5405_set_otg_en/...c052b7bc). The rodata
#     anchor 0xc0daf358 named in the spec is BSS (state vars, incl. the
#     is_aw87559 flag @0xc0daf460 read by is_aw87559_exit @c056f2bc), not a pin
#     pool. Fork keeps its a106 GPIO93 entry (no Q5 function collides with it;
#     documented in the report).
#  4. Leds hygiene (cust_leds.c): red/green/button PMIC ISINK1/0/2 ->
#     MT65XX_LED_MODE_NONE, -1 — the blob's get_cust_led_list array
#     @0xc0b5fb7c carries NONE,-1 for all six non-LCD entries. The
#     lcd-backlight entry stays byte-identical (mode5 = CUST_BLS_PWM,
#     disp_bls_set_backlight == blob 0xc03a743c; PWM support 256 == blob
#     @c004e2e8).
#  5. Keypad (cust_kpd.h): the blob's compiled kpd_keymap rodata @0xc08d0e34 =
#     {[0]=114 VOLUMEDOWN, [1]=115 VOLUMEUP, 0...} vs a106 {[1]=VOLUP,[2]=VOLDOWN}
#     — the matrix wiring differs by one, so the port IS required ("expected
#     match" did not hold; recovery/DL keys keep their meanings: hw1=VOLUP
#     unchanged). kpd_set_debounce(1024) @c04a4990 == KPD_KEY_DEBOUNCE 1024
#     (unchanged); MTK_PMIC_PWR_KEY=8 is PMIC-chip-level, matches.
#  6. RTC BBPU / vibrator: NO PORT — hal_rtc_bbpu_pwdn GPIO triple =
#     GPIO_SRCLKEN_PIN = GPIO37|0x80000025 @c0493880 == the fork's
#     include/linux/pmic6326_sw.h:61 define (GPIO37); vibrator cust struct
#     @0xc0b5fb70 = {50, 9, 0x5} == the fork's cust_vibrator.c byte-for-byte.
#  6b. SPEAKER (re-decode correction to the spec's §2 speaker row): the Q5's
#     Speaker_Init/Sound_Speaker_Turnon program GPIO8|0x80000008 (a106: GPIO6),
#     gated on is_aw87559_exit() so amp-fitted units (the fork's D13/D14 i2c
#     path) never drive it. GPIO_SPEAKER_EN_PIN GPIO6->GPIO8 hygiene port
#     (cust_gpio_usage.h); no compiled consumer changes in this tree.
#  7. Camera re-check (assertion-only per design): main CMRST/CMPDN GPIO9/10 ==
#     blob pinSet rows @0xc083c170+0x00/+0x10. SUB-CAMERA DIVERGES — re-decode
#     found the blob at GPIO16/GPIO18 (@+0x20/+0x30) vs the a106 lineage's
#     GPIO3/GPIO4, which are exactly the Q5's card-detect and ACCDET pads -- two
#     drivers would fight over the same lines once items 1-2 land. Ported
#     CMRST1 GPIO3->GPIO16, CMPDN1 GPIO4->GPIO18 (cust_gpio_usage.h). This
#     extension of the row's "verify-only" wording is flagged prominently in
#     forge-m4-report §4 (Bob may veto with a 2-line revert).
#
# NOT PORTED (per spec §3.2 — documented, do not re-chase): cust_gpio_boot.h
# (inert: 4 consumers, all unbuilt), PMIC cust/eint (empty/equal, asserted),
# TE/LANE/LCM-reset (closed by D18 + register-only evidence), clocks/PLL (no
# board table), partitions/touch/LCM (D18/D17).
#
# PARITY + PRECEDENCE GATES (build/62_kernel_delta_board.sh): the D20 constants
# asserted in source; the compiled proof = hal_kpd.o .data {[0]=114,[1]=115},
# kd_camera_hw.o rodata carries 0x80000010/0x80000012 and NOT 0x80000003/4,
# sd.o registration immediate 3 (was 8) + debounce arg 0 (was 1), accdet.o
# immediate 4 (was 0) + 0x80000004 GPIO arg (was 0x80000000).
---

