+# headers (cust_eint.h / cust_gpio_usage.h / cust_kpd.h / ...) from the
+# a106-provenanced codegen.dws into $(DRVGEN_OUT)/inc at EVERY build (archprepare
+# runs tools/dct/DrvGen; scripts/drvgen/drvgen.mk). Without the -I added below,
+# the O-dir copies shadow the source-tree headers (the only /inc dir before
+# D20), so editing arch/arm/mach-mt6582/q5/dct/dct/inc/*.h would be a silent
+# no-op. The D20-pinned Q5 board values live in those source headers; this
+# extra -I (placed BEFORE the $(DRVGEN_OUT)/inc line) makes them win include
+# precedence. Overriding headers: cust_eint.h, cust_gpio_usage.h, cust_kpd.h --
+# every other header still resolves from DrvGen and stays bit-identical to
+# today. build/62_kernel_delta_board.sh asserts the D20 constants AND proves
+# the precedence took effect on the compiled objects ( forge-m4-report ).
